{"kind":"assert","text":"Grow archive HTTP-response diagnostic, early Source assessment by checker session 44e8, read from Git at 020c76f997 (tree 61bc72e3), branch builder/archive-http-response-20261023, on Main 12d30573. Not the formal review. I read the primary note first, then the production diff (http-read.ts, archive-parent-read-diagnostic.ts) and both test diffs.\n\nNo required finding.\n- The response guard is unchanged. The refusal gains frozen, fixed categories only: status class, a redirected flag, URL relation (empty, exact or changed), and a media category. No status text, URL, header value or body is kept.\n- The annotation is best effort. A throwing getter cannot replace the refusal, and the body is still cancelled.\n- The pass-owned snapshot carries the detail with the same fence as the advertisement detail.\nArchitecture, Security and Simplification are clear, apart from the points below.\n\nTwo nonblocking points. The first can save one deploy round:\nP3-1. The case of the media type is not classified. The guard and the classifier both compare exact lowercase strings. Media types are case-insensitive (RFC 9110 section 8.3.1). A reply of \"Application/X-Git-Upload-Pack-Result\" is refused and labelled \"other\", so the next tail would not show that case is the cause. Suggest: classify a lowercased copy of the type in the diagnostic only, or add a category such as \"upload-pack-result-case\". Keep the guard exactly as it is, unless the planner then decides to relax it.\nP3-2. The new interface was inserted between the old comment \"Fixed diagnostic words only…\" and AdvertisementRefusalDetail. Two doc comments now stand together, and the advertisement interface has lost its own. Move the old comment back above AdvertisementRefusalDetail.\n\nThe formal review waits for the owning checks, the control, the gate and the review request at the exact head."}